$DIR/main.p:18:37: cannot convert 3 (untyped int constant) to owner type MyFd: it holds a new sys.Fd, which only package sys can make
    An owner owns memory or another resource and releases it when it is dropped,
    so it moves instead of being copied. MyFd is defined from the owner type
    sys.Fd, so a new MyFd holds a new sys.Fd. Converting an untyped int into a
    MyFd is allowed only where converting it into a sys.Fd is allowed too, and
    only the package that declares sys.Fd may make one, where its invariants are
    kept.
    Convert a value that is already a sys.Fd, made by the package that declares
    it:
        MyFd(sys.FdValue)
    (see "Conversions" in the Plutonium spec, section 11.24)
    (run "pluto explain E3212" for a longer explanation)

